article-extractor.user:
Page URL: {{url}}
Fields: {{fields}}

Extract the main article from this page. `text` is the article body (first 1200 characters is enough), `excerpt` is one sentence, `headings` is an array of section headings, `authors` and `tags` are arrays.

{{page}}

ecommerce-product.user:
Page URL: {{url}}
Fields: {{fields}}

Extract the product on this page. `price` is a number, `currency` an ISO code, `availability` one of in_stock, out_of_stock, preorder, unknown, `variants` an array of {name, price}. Prefer JSON-LD Product data when present.

{{page}}

company-enrichment.user:
Page URL: {{url}}
Fields: {{fields}}

Build a company profile from this homepage. `socials` is an object keyed by network (twitter, linkedin, github, youtube, instagram, facebook) with URLs, `emails` and `phones` are arrays, `techHints` is an array of technologies mentioned, `employeeCountHint` is a string if the page hints at size.

{{page}}

faq-extractor.user:
Page URL: {{url}}
Fields: {{fields}}

Extract every question-and-answer pair on this page. `faqs` is an array of {position, question, answer, source} where source is "jsonld" if it came from schema.org FAQPage data, otherwise "heuristic". Keep answers under 300 characters each.

{{page}}

contact-info-extractor.user:
Page URL: {{url}}
Fields: {{fields}}

Find the organization's contact details on this page. `emails`, `phones`, `addresses` are arrays of strings; `socials` is an array of URLs; `contactFormUrl` is a URL or null.

{{page}}

github-repo.user:
Page URL: {{url}}
Fields: {{fields}}

Extract repository metadata from this GitHub page. `stars` and `forks` are integers (expand 1.2k to 1200), `topics` is an array of strings, `latestRelease` is the tag name or null.

{{page}}

job-posting.user:
Page URL: {{url}}
Fields: {{fields}}

Extract the job posting on this page. `departments` is an array, `content` is a plain-text summary of responsibilities and requirements under 800 characters.

{{page}}

docs-page.user:
Page URL: {{url}}
Fields: {{fields}}

This is a documentation page. `breadcrumbs` and `headings` are arrays of strings in page order, `codeBlockCount` is an integer estimate, `sectionPath` is the doc section inferred from the URL, `summary` is two sentences describing what the page teaches.

{{page}}
